    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0842" n="746" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500a4/191: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-23T18:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 23—1:11
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>313. Following telegram received from consul, Dairen.</p>
                <pb facs="0843" n="747" xml:id="pg747"/>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“September 23, 11 a.m. Referring to the American Government’s apparent
                        refusal to permit Far Eastern Republic to send delegates to Washington
                            Conference,<anchor n="52" xml:id="d706-f1"/> Yurin inquires if there is
                        any objection to send trade mission from Chita.</p>
                </quote>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d706-f1" n="52" xml:id="d706-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 545, Sept. 17, to the Ambassador in Great Britain, <ref
                        target="frus1921v01#pg_69">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p.
                        69</ref>.</p>
            </note>
